  "answer": "This crash has been reported before, but I found no fix and no workaround in those tickets. terminal#17246 is the same drag-merge crash with a fault in Microsoft.Terminal.Control.dll. In that ticket, a tab that is torn off or merged is left detached, and a null pointer is dereferenced. Part of that crash takes down the whole process. terminal#19383 is the closest match. It is a WindowsTerminal.exe 0xc0000005 in Microsoft.Terminal.Control.dll when dragging a tab to merge windows. WinDbg put the fault in the render thread, in AtlasEngine::PaintCursor. A later comment there reports the same failure bucket on a newer build. Please add your report to #19383. Include your 1.24.2605.12001 build, the fault offset 0x2c924, and the details about heavy scrollback and the RADAR_PRE_LEAK warning. Don't attach the dump publicly, because it contains scrollback. Tell the maintainers it's available and offer it through a private channel, such as a Feedback Hub upload. As a precaution until it is fixed, avoid dragging tabs between windows. You could also save your work first, or use fewer windows and smaller scrollback."
